Bloub — the drawn companion bundled with Grok Chief

This folder holds no artwork. The character is code: `keystone/Bloub.js`
computes its outline, its eyes and its decor every frame, and `pet.json`
only says which renderer to use and how large it prefers to be.

That code is a port of bloub (https://github.com/jeremy-prt/bloub),
Copyright (c) 2026 Jérémy Perret, MIT — an SVG recreation of the x.ai bot
avatar, whose fourteen states, silhouettes, easings and eye geometry were
measured frame by frame off the reference video. The port changes the
output, not the geometry: it emits points and matrices for a QML Canvas
where the original emits SVG path strings for a browser. Every constant,
easing and schedule is carried over unaltered, and a test checks that
claim against the original engine rather than trusting it.

`keystone/BloubFit.js` is generated, not written: `tools/build-eyefit`
runs bloub's own eye-fit solver and prints the table it produces.

Grok Chief is not affiliated with x.ai and does not reproduce anything of
theirs beyond what bloub already did — the shape of an avatar. See the
repository's `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.
